{
  "_comment": [
    "Annotation predicate IRIs recognised when extracting preferred labels, synonyms, and",
    "lexical annotations from an ontology. These are EXTERNAL IDENTIFIERS: each string must",
    "match the RDF byte-for-byte, so they are data rather than authored source. They live in",
    "this file, and not in ontology/access.py, so that adding or retiring a vocabulary is a",
    "data change. Order is irrelevant (each group is loaded into a set); duplicates are",
    "harmless. 'lexical_extra' is unioned with the other two groups to form the lexical set.",
    "Classification rule: a predicate goes in the group matching its SEMANTICS, not its",
    "vocabulary — definition/gloss predicates (e.g. oboInOwl#hasDefinition) are lexical",
    "context, never synonyms (a whole definition sentence is not an alternative name), and",
    "preferred-label predicates belong in 'preferred_label' whichever vocabulary they come",
    "from. Moving a predicate between groups changes prompt content (see convention 3)."
  ],
